A||||1||BOILERMAKER||Automatic Owners - Good PM action to take||||1||
Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||10-01-2000||10:19 PM||||I was having a quirk (or was it an anomoly) with my automatic shuddering only when in the torque lockup range of the drive.  Not wanting to change out the converter lock-up solenoid, I took the easy route and changed the tranny filter and replaced the lost fluid.  Now, it has gotten rid or the shudder  for the short term, and it still may be the solenoid, but I have never changed the filter (probably was the original) nor had I ever changed any fluid in the tranny.<P>This is a good PM action to take since all of our cars are getting up there in age.  I'm not saying that this action will resolve all problems, but could be a chance for some of us to stay away from costly problems down the road.<P>I know that a lot of people already know this, but wanted to bring it up again to keep it fresh.||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-02-2000||03:52 PM||||So it's a good PM action, but what if I'm a morning person?  Wouldn't it be a good action then, too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ?<P>Actually, I'm glad you posted this, because it's surprising how many times we forget to try the simple stuff first.  Glad you had success with this, and hope it continues  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !    ||||reg||12
